Step 0 now points to a viable native family, but not the naïve “endpoint pair plus listed vertices.” I’m evaluating the paper’s CGL-style non-backtracking walk encoding (Sections 2–3) and its product-path construction (Lemma 3 / Algorithm 1). The key distinction is that planted short paths admit meet-in-the-middle attacks, so the shipping path length and field size must place both that attack and the paper’s \(\widetilde O(\sqrt p)\) elliptic path finder out of range; otherwise Track A would be false.
