codex
Step 0 decision: this is a Track A family, not Track B and not a rejection. I’ll use the paper’s native CGL preimage/path problem (Sections 2–3), inverse-generate a non-backtracking \(2\)-isogeny walk, and publish only its encoded source state and endpoint. The witness is the bounded kernel-choice word; exact verification replays Vélu’s degree-2 quotient formula over \(\mathbb F_{p^2}\). The paper’s known algorithms remain exponential here: fixed-length meet-in-the-middle is exponential in half the word length, while general elliptic path finding is \(\widetilde O(\sqrt p)\). No auxiliary torsion-point images—the feature behind the SIDH break—will be published.
