The exact arithmetic prototype is working: planted words verify at all four presets, the demo has three valid preimages (so the checker correctly accepts alternatives), all five corruption classes receive distinct rejection reasons, the capped meet-in-the-middle attack solves the demo, and affine/Frobenius relabellings preserve both the canonical key and a carried witness. I’m starting the full 200,000-sample and eight-seed adversarial run now; this is the expensive validation pass.
