+NOTES = """
+Section 4 supplies the PPAV, Lagrangian-kernel, and (ell,...,ell)-isogeny
+definitions.  Section 5 identifies a genus-2 PPAV as either a genus-2 Jacobian
+or a product of elliptic curves.  Lemma 1 proves that equal-parity factor paths
+compose to a product path.  Section 2 defines fixed-length path finding and
+states the best generic elliptic costs; Theorem 1 and its proof show that the
+general genus-2 problem has a ~O(p) attack and that product nodes recurse to
+elliptic path finding.  Thus this is Track B: an algorithm exists and is
+reported, rather than hidden as a Track-A claim.
+
+Generation is inverse: sample both non-backtracking factor words, compose
+their exact Velu quotients, then publish the endpoint product.  The same secret
+word is also carried by a common change of variables between two legitimate
+Weierstrass presentations of the target factors.  This is the compact route.
+Plants and random candidates use exactly the same 9*4^(n-1) word distribution.
+Endpoint-coefficient, greedy, random-restart, and raw-coefficient attacks were
+included because earlier versions exposed the planted word through position or
+coefficient size.  The primary target models now have a common uniformly
+conditioned square scale and the decoders tested in those attacks do not use
+the mixed-radix invariant.
+""".strip()
